{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/377907-aberrant-ideas","id":377907,"title":"Aberrant Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-22T02:25:03-08:00","id":377907,"title":"Aberrant Ideas","content":"So I've been rolling ideas for an Aberrant story, but I've been having trouble coming up with any that allow for a variety of character types that would work together.<br /> <br /> So, what story ideas have you used in the past? Figure this can become the equivalent to those story seed threads on the old forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T03:03:48-08:00","id":377918,"title":"","content":"I ran a PC driven rewrite to the storyline presented in Aberrant as backstory canon, but I'm sure this has been done. Another idea I wanted to run uses the marvel universe's setting;<br /> Question: How would the X-men's villains effectively cripple them for the rest of time? Answer: Manipulate the US government into legalizing mutants to such a degree that they are mandated to build, fund, staff, and maintain an actual &quot;mutant academy&quot; in every single state. Yes it would be borderline segregation, but the public is almost assuredly going to go with it to keep their &quot;normal&quot; children safe, and insure that random mutants don't randomly just blow stuff up. Xavier would be scouted (harassed or drafted more like) by the government to find staff for all these institutions, tying up every X-man with a degree (less than you'd think), and severely distracting those without. In all that legitimate and positive bureaucracy, they'd be completely helpless when villain X launched the next heinous (and subtle) plot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T04:11:15-08:00","id":377941,"title":"","content":"I started an Aberrant campaign a while back, mostly to run during breaks in the Trinity modules, I simply borrowed the idea of the Trinity Continuum as I understand it and had the first story be set off by a USAF bomber from the 1950's popping through an anomaly (which was over lake michigan) then having the characters drawn together by their separate stories being related to a transdimensional alien invasion. I drew a lot of inspiration from Avengers, Cthulhu Mythos, Threshold (tv show) and Doctor Who. Heck I am even running it as being continuous with the Trinity timeline I am running.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Man's unfailing capacity to believe what he prefers to be true rather than what the evidence shows to be likely and possible has always astounded me. We long for a caring Universe which will save us from our childish mistakes, and in the face of mountains of evidence to the contrary we will pin all our hopes on the slimmest of doubts. God has not been proven not to exist, therefore he must exist.</i> <b>--Academician Prokhor Zakharov</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3246-galaxy-master-zhad","name":"Galaxy Master Zhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T10:24:17-08:00","id":378163,"title":"","content":"Since I am a big fan of huge sprawling chronicles that turn into epic sagas, I have started characters off in Adventure! and then had their descendants show up in Aberrant. From there, I used those same novas as aberrants in Trinity. All set to the backdrop that the Doyen were the ones that inspired Hammersmith.<br /> His device was meant to terraform the Earth for the Doyen to be able to survive in the quantum/psion spectrum on Earth but another alien race decided to sabotage that. The aliens would inhabit some people and used their influence to try to poison the Earth's radiation. They were the Arachne Society in Adventure! and the heroes opposed their evil attempts to, as the heroes knew it, destroy the world.<br /> In Aberrant, the main antagonist was a Psion who had been sent back in time through the Venezuela Phenomenon to try to stop Divis Mal from doing the whole Galatea thing. He failed and then he was going to try to bring down the Teragen movement. The players were, of course, Teragen.<br /> Lastly, in Trinity, the players were the ones sent to speak to the Coalition. At some point, they would be trapped on the ship and then dealt with the politics of the various races there. It eventually was discovered that the leaders of the various races in the Coalition were all being controlled by the Anansi (the alien race that opposed the Doyens) and that they were there to save the Earth. The problem is, the Doyen activated some programming inside of the Psions who had been dunked in the Prometheus Chambers and turned all of them against the players and the Coalition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T17:44:23-08:00","id":378543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/377907-aberrant-ideas?p=378163#post378163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I am a big fan of huge sprawling chronicles that turn into epic sagas, I have started characters off in Adventure! and then had their descendants show up in Aberrant. From there, I used those same novas as aberrants in Trinity. All set to the backdrop that the Doyen were the ones that inspired Hammersmith.<br /> His device was meant to terraform the Earth for the Doyen to be able to survive in the quantum/psion spectrum on Earth but another alien race decided to sabotage that. The aliens would inhabit some people and used their influence to try to poison the Earth's radiation. They were the Arachne Society in Adventure! and the heroes opposed their evil attempts to, as the heroes knew it, destroy the world.<br /> In Aberrant, the main antagonist was a Psion who had been sent back in time through the Venezuela Phenomenon to try to stop Divis Mal from doing the whole Galatea thing. He failed and then he was going to try to bring down the Teragen movement. The players were, of course, Teragen.<br /> Lastly, in Trinity, the players were the ones sent to speak to the Coalition. At some point, they would be trapped on the ship and then dealt with the politics of the various races there. It eventually was discovered that the leaders of the various races in the Coalition were all being controlled by the Anansi (the alien race that opposed the Doyens) and that they were there to save the Earth. The problem is, the Doyen activated some programming inside of the Psions who had been dunked in the Prometheus Chambers and turned all of them against the players and the Coalition.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... I understood approximately none of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T18:07:52-08:00","id":378557,"title":"","content":"Sorry about that. The Aeoniverse was my favorite line out of anything WW ever published and so I read everything I could find of it. The post references things outside of Aberrant. It references elements from Aberrant's sequel, Adventure! and it's prequel, Trinity. <br /> Dr. Hammersmith was a scientist whose experiment exploded in his face and it created the heroic age of the 20's. <br /> The Doyen are an alien race that had manipulated humanity to give them psionic powers because the quantum powers of the novas wrecked havoc with the Doyen. They gave the first psions devices called Prometheus Chambers to help let other people with psionic powers manifest those powers.<br /> The Venezuela Phenomenon was in the Asia Ascendant book (that never was published) and detailed out how there is something going on in Venezuela to make things go all wonky when it comes to psionic powers. <br /> The Coalition is a group of aliens in a large ship that is currently heading to Earth and something that people are not sure if they are on humanity's side or if they are just novas.<br /> I don't know how much you know about the game Trinity, but in the future, the novas go insane and start to destroy the Earth until they got kicked off (or left depending on what you want to read into things). They finally come back and they are pissed. The Psions are the ones who have to try to stop these mentally and physically mutated beings.<br /> The part about the Anansi and Arachne Society are my own stuff and the other things referenced are all in Aberrant so I hope you got those references. My bad for losing you. I didn't know how much you did or did not know about the Aeoniverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T19:17:18-08:00","id":378606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/377907-aberrant-ideas?p=378557#post378557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry about that. The Aeoniverse was my favorite line out of anything WW ever published and so I read everything I could find of it. The post references things outside of Aberrant. It references elements from Aberrant's sequel, Adventure! and it's prequel, Trinity.<br /> Dr. Hammersmith was a scientist whose experiment exploded in his face and it created the heroic age of the 20's.<br /> ...<br /> <u>The Venezuela Phenomenon was in the Asia Ascendant book (that never was published)</u> and detailed out how there is something going on in Venezuela to make things go all wonky when it comes to psionic powers.<br /> ...<br /> The part about the Anansi and Arachne Society are my own stuff and the other things referenced are all in Aberrant so I hope you got those references. My bad for losing you. I didn't know how much you did or did not know about the Aeoniverse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gah, I had enough trouble keeping up with the books that <i>did</i> exist, now I need to read books that don't in order to keep up? Where's my Unseen University library card... I kid, I kid. I figured it was from the other lines, just I don't know anything about them.<br /> <br /> I always wondered how the 20s game worked, since novas are allegedly created by that satellite exploding (although I vaguely remember something about that not being the case). Turns out a <i>different</i> experiment exploded. I'm noticing a pattern <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T06:56:19-08:00","id":378992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/377907-aberrant-ideas?p=378557#post378557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Venezuela Phenomenon was in the Asia Ascendant book (that never was published) and detailed out how there is something going on in Venezuela to make things go all wonky when it comes to psionic powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>However it was made available, and can still be downloaded online here: <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/File:AsiaAscendant.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/File:AsiaAscendant.pdf</a><br /> <br /> My understanding is that the line was cancelled before it got released, but developer Bruce Baugh came to an agreement to release its contents as a free document. Its considered by many to be canon because it was scheduled and 'done' even if not officially published - for others its a bit of a gray area. Is definitely worth a read though (also, free!).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T07:01:59-08:00","id":378998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/377907-aberrant-ideas?p=378606#post378606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gah, I had enough trouble keeping up with the books that <i>did</i> exist</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an excellent 'Story so far' write up in the softcover version of Trinity that covers the Aberrant era through to the 2120's, with a focus on the later years and some explanation of the run up to the Aberrant War. It doesn't really cover the 1920's though. I'm 99% sure this version on DTRPG has the Story So Far in it (someone please correct me if I'm wrong about that): <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/3407/Trinity-Rulebook?it=1&amp;filters=0_0_10110_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...=0_0_10110_0_0</a><br /> <br /> You may also find this of interest, its unofficial, but has plenty of timeline stuff of note: <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Timeline_%28TU%29\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Timeline_%28TU%29</a><br /> <br /> Hope that helps.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T07:39:44-08:00","id":379022,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the suggestion, but I'm of the opinion that the canon is kind of restrictive, so I'm trying to ignore it as hard as I can (I'll pay attention to the broad strokes, ie what's in the core Aberrant book, but I'm not feeling overly compelled to read the others)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T21:36:06-08:00","id":379829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/377907-aberrant-ideas?p=378557#post378557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It references elements from Aberrant's sequel, Adventure! and it's prequel, Trinity.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://media.giphy.com/media/mjCaQoS4O7jEs/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T07:06:21-08:00","id":380957,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it was:<ul><li><b>Published in 1997:</b> Aeon (later under the name Trinity) - Set in early 2120s</li> <li><b>Published in 1999:</b> Aberrant - Set in late 1990s and 2000s</li> <li><b>Published in 2001: </b>Adventure! - Set in 1920s</li> </ul>Aeon's rapidly heading to its 20 year anniversary.... damn. O_o.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T09:22:17-08:00","id":381054,"title":"","content":"It depends on if you want to go by published date or setting........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T17:16:14-08:00","id":381450,"title":"","content":"To determine if something is a sequel or prequel, go by release date and then setting. <b>Trinity</b> is set later and released earlier, so <b>Aberrant</b> is its prequel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","user":"Craig Oxbrow","date":". 01-26-2015, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T17:42:42-08:00","id":381461,"title":"","content":"Star Wars Episodes 1-3 are called the &quot;prequel trilogy&quot; because they're set before the Original Trilogy (Eps 4-6), despite being released 20 years later. Where release date and setting clash, I'm unaware of any case where prequel/sequel doesn't refer to setting over release date.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T10:45:14-08:00","id":382137,"title":"","content":"can we has world war 2?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T15:25:20-08:00","id":382376,"title":"","content":"Editing for clairty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T17:27:45-08:00","id":382500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/377907-aberrant-ideas?p=382137#post382137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can we has world war 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you phrase that in terms of a story idea for Aberrant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T17:49:25-08:00","id":382513,"title":"","content":"Well, in the information for Aeoniverse (the combined conintuity of Trinity, Aberrant and Adevnture!) 2.0, they have said that we will have more than just those three timelines/settings to play around in. In fact, IIRC, they said there would be seven. One of them, the 1980's from the sound of it, will be included in the corebook for the whole line. I say 1980's but that is only because it sounded like that in the description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T19:54:14-08:00","id":382630,"title":"","content":"Actually, the corebook will contain present-day setting information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T23:56:24-08:00","id":382779,"title":"","content":"I thought so but I seem to read some hype about it setting it &quot;last week&quot; sort of time in contrast to the &quot;next week&quot; feel that Aberrant had. But if it is modern day (2015) then that is great. It means we get to map out things and plot out our own futures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T01:05:31-08:00","id":382811,"title":"","content":"The Trinity Continuum core is going to be modern day. The Aberrant core is, last I heard, supposed to pick up about 2028 (and, like the old Aberrant core, will pick up some time after the Novas first emerge).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T06:03:25-08:00","id":384932,"title":"","content":"I ditched 90% of the Aberrant cannon and ran a game similar to Heroes in power levels. The Hammersmith experiment in my setting was a secret project paralleling the Trinity nuclear test. It was run by Oppenheimer, Einstein, Tesla, and others. The modern day PCs are the descendents of the people caught in the energy wave from the explosion. Secret societies and corporations have come out of the powers that the PCs grand parents and great grandparents attained during the experiment. The PCs were put together by one of those people and now their on a path to discover what happened all those years ago. <br /> <br /> The PCs could not choose to start with a Quantum higher than 3 and no higher than level 2 powers. Been running it about a year and they all love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}